t week of that crowdfunding  effort the state raised  something like 450 000 um  and since we're talking about costs the  operation  lone star that they have going on right  now is costing two and a half million  dollars per week uh  and that's primarily in you know  overtime for the  crews that they have down here that's  housing them  in this area bringing them in from  elsewhere and putting them up in hotels  so that's an expensive operation as well  the landowners and you referenced the  that you need  some permission for this border wall on  private property but there have been a  lot of land owners who have  have had enough i mean they've had their  their property overrun by people coming  across the border  right yeah and we you know talk with  people on  fox business and fox news all the time  who are landowners  ranchers business owners who deal with  it all the time and they see these large  groups coming through their property  you know one of the challenges may be  they might own the property close to the  border but that doesn't mean they own  the the property  right on the border or even if they do  you know that maybe there's just not a  as much activity  uh in in terms of construction because  they're focusing their efforts  on other areas at the moment but  certainly there are a lot of people  in this stretch of the border who you  know who have had enough of it  especially lately  because if you look at the numbers it's  a huge increase from  you know a year ago grady trimble fox  business network correspondent  at the border in la jolla texas great to  talk to you thanks so much for joining  us grady  thank you dave  [Music]  [Applause]  jason in the house the jason chaffetz  podcast  dive deeper than the headlines in the  party lines as i take on  american life politics and entertainment  subscribe now on  foxnewspodcast.com or wherever you  download podcasts  subscribe to this podcast at  foxnewspodcasts.com  it's time for your fox news commenta